{"events":[{"tStartMs":80,"dDurationMs":3920,"segs":[{"utf8":"So here is the thing; if you have a need for something nowadays then"}]},{"tStartMs":4000,"dDurationMs":5600,"segs":[{"utf8":"you can pretty easily get your hands on a perfectly fitting product which can be for"}]},{"tStartMs":9600,"dDurationMs":5960,"segs":[{"utf8":"example a video door bell or wireless temperature sensor or something else."}]},{"tStartMs":15560,"dDurationMs":7240,"segs":[{"utf8":"But sometimes your need or problem is so niche, that there is no good buy option out there."}]},{"tStartMs":22800,"dDurationMs":5280,"segs":[{"utf8":"Case in point would be the cistern in my garden which is basically a huge"}]},{"tStartMs":28080,"dDurationMs":5880,"segs":[{"utf8":"reservoir put into the ground into which all the rain water from my roofs flow."}]},{"tStartMs":33960,"dDurationMs":6520,"segs":[{"utf8":"As you can see it is filled to the brim right now and since there is a submersible pump in there,"}]},{"tStartMs":40480,"dDurationMs":7320,"segs":[{"utf8":"I can simply power that and water my garden with rain water which is pretty awesome."}]},{"tStartMs":47800,"dDurationMs":6280,"segs":[{"utf8":"Only problem is that I have no idea how much water is left in this reservoir meaning I"}]},{"tStartMs":54080,"dDurationMs":5640,"segs":[{"utf8":"need something like a water level sensor. But no matter how long I searched online,"}]},{"tStartMs":59720,"dDurationMs":6320,"segs":[{"utf8":"I could either only find not suitable options or way too expensive ones."}]},{"tStartMs":66040,"dDurationMs":7080,"segs":[{"utf8":"So in this episode of DIY or Buy, I will not only show you why available buy options"}]},{"tStartMs":73120,"dDurationMs":7440,"segs":[{"utf8":"sometimes kind of suck, but also create my own DIY alternative which will hopefully be"}]},{"tStartMs":80560,"dDurationMs":9360,"segs":[{"utf8":"functional and a lot cheaper. Let's get started!"}]},{"tStartMs":93120,"dDurationMs":6320,"segs":[{"utf8":"This video is sponsored by JLCPCB who are currently running a promotion meaning you get"}]},{"tStartMs":99440,"dDurationMs":10080,"segs":[{"utf8":"a $20 discount for their 6-Layer PCBs including free via-in pad and free 2u ENIG finish. And in"}]},{"tStartMs":109520,"dDurationMs":6560,"segs":[{"utf8":"case you are wondering what via-in-pad means, then let me tell you that you can literally place vias"}]},{"tStartMs":116080,"dDurationMs":8280,"segs":[{"utf8":"directly in pads which shorts traces, saves board space and solves routing challenges. So give them"}]},{"tStartMs":124360,"dDurationMs":7760,"segs":[{"utf8":"a try. Other than that JLCPCB is still holding their Mid-Year-Promotion; so click the links"}]},{"tStartMs":132120,"dDurationMs":9960,"segs":[{"utf8":"below to get a chance to win awesome prizes and coupons worth up to 250$. Don't miss out on this!"}]},{"tStartMs":142080,"dDurationMs":5653,"segs":[{"utf8":"Now first off let's have a closer look at the buy options and here it seems like they"}]},{"tStartMs":147733,"dDurationMs":5587,"segs":[{"utf8":"are either using an ultrasonic sensor or a hydrostatic sensor."}]},{"tStartMs":153320,"dDurationMs":6120,"segs":[{"utf8":"And let me tell you that the latter one really feels like high quality with its stainless"}]},{"tStartMs":159440,"dDurationMs":6120,"segs":[{"utf8":"steel sensor head and rather heavy weight. The idea of this sensor is that it measure"}]},{"tStartMs":165560,"dDurationMs":6120,"segs":[{"utf8":"the underwater pressure which gets bigger and bigger the deeper the sensor goes."}]},{"tStartMs":171680,"dDurationMs":12520,"segs":[{"utf8":"My version here outputs 0 to 3.3V over a range or depth of 2m which equals around 0.165V per 10cm."}]},{"tStartMs":184200,"dDurationMs":6680,"segs":[{"utf8":"To verify that, I powered this thing with 5V and then had a look at the output pin."}]},{"tStartMs":190880,"dDurationMs":6040,"segs":[{"utf8":"And yes; it seems to be pretty accurate and due to its heavy duty construction,"}]},{"tStartMs":196920,"dDurationMs":6400,"segs":[{"utf8":"it is often used for industrial applications or with more aggressive liquids."}]},{"tStartMs":203320,"dDurationMs":5440,"segs":[{"utf8":"That is why such a sensor is not really cheap and therefore products that come"}]},{"tStartMs":208760,"dDurationMs":5920,"segs":[{"utf8":"with it are obviously also not cheap. But thankfully there are also these"}]},{"tStartMs":214680,"dDurationMs":7240,"segs":[{"utf8":"ultrasonic sensors whose non waterproof alternative is pretty popular I would say."}]},{"tStartMs":221920,"dDurationMs":6720,"segs":[{"utf8":"The way this works is that one of these speakers sends out a 40kHz Ultrasonic Wave"}]},{"tStartMs":228640,"dDurationMs":6680,"segs":[{"utf8":"which bounces back once it hits an object and the other speaker then notices that."}]},{"tStartMs":235320,"dDurationMs":5840,"segs":[{"utf8":"And since we know how fast the sound wave travelled and how long it took to return,"}]},{"tStartMs":241160,"dDurationMs":4480,"segs":[{"utf8":"we can very simply calculate the distance to the object."}]},{"tStartMs":245640,"dDurationMs":6800,"segs":[{"utf8":"I mean it is so simple that such sensors are often included in Arduino beginners kits and"}]},{"tStartMs":252440,"dDurationMs":6840,"segs":[{"utf8":"the wiring for them is done in seconds as well as writing a short piece of code for them."}]},{"tStartMs":259280,"dDurationMs":6760,"segs":[{"utf8":"And by doing some testing here, I can say that the measured distances are pretty accurate and"}]},{"tStartMs":266040,"dDurationMs":6280,"segs":[{"utf8":"definitely good enough for my cistern which by the way works with this sensor because water"}]},{"tStartMs":272320,"dDurationMs":6000,"segs":[{"utf8":"also reflects the ultrasonic sound wave. But of course when it comes to water,"}]},{"tStartMs":278320,"dDurationMs":4920,"segs":[{"utf8":"then we should use this waterproof ultrasonic sensor which now only"}]},{"tStartMs":283240,"dDurationMs":7760,"segs":[{"utf8":"comes with one so called transducer that can obviously acts as a transmitter and receiver."}]},{"tStartMs":291000,"dDurationMs":6280,"segs":[{"utf8":"And wiring this one up is pretty much the same deal as before; I mean we can even use the same"}]},{"tStartMs":297280,"dDurationMs":9120,"segs":[{"utf8":"code and get pretty similar good results; except that this time the minimum distance is 20cm."}]},{"tStartMs":306400,"dDurationMs":5880,"segs":[{"utf8":"And best off, this sensor is dirt cheap in comparison to the one before."}]},{"tStartMs":312280,"dDurationMs":4040,"segs":[{"utf8":"But when they are featured in products, then they are either too expensive if"}]},{"tStartMs":316320,"dDurationMs":7120,"segs":[{"utf8":"I want a customizable wireless solution or they want me to mount it in some place weird."}]},{"tStartMs":323440,"dDurationMs":4560,"segs":[{"utf8":"So can we DIY a solution? To find that out, I firstly"}]},{"tStartMs":328000,"dDurationMs":7240,"segs":[{"utf8":"had a closer look inside my cistern and realized that at a water level of 94cm,"}]},{"tStartMs":335240,"dDurationMs":8400,"segs":[{"utf8":"the reservoir is at max capacity with 10.000L. I also found this removable screw here which"}]},{"tStartMs":343640,"dDurationMs":7360,"segs":[{"utf8":"is a perfect spot to mount the sensor and at a height of around 30cm above the max water level,"}]},{"tStartMs":351000,"dDurationMs":8360,"segs":[{"utf8":"it should be in range of what the sensor can do. That means a distance of 30cm would represent 100%"}]},{"tStartMs":359360,"dDurationMs":10920,"segs":[{"utf8":"water and 124cm would represent 0% water left. And luckily for me I also got a tube here through"}]},{"tStartMs":370280,"dDurationMs":7000,"segs":[{"utf8":"which the power wire for the pump travels into my garage and needless to say there is lots of"}]},{"tStartMs":377280,"dDurationMs":6600,"segs":[{"utf8":"space inside this tube that we can use. So next I pushed a string in there in"}]},{"tStartMs":383880,"dDurationMs":4480,"segs":[{"utf8":"order to ultimately determine what distance the sensor wire has to"}]},{"tStartMs":388360,"dDurationMs":10400,"segs":[{"utf8":"bridge and as it turns out it is around 3.3m Sadly though the sensor wire is only 2.5m long;"}]},{"tStartMs":398760,"dDurationMs":5760,"segs":[{"utf8":"but no problem for me is what I thought; I can simply extend that."}]},{"tStartMs":404520,"dDurationMs":6720,"segs":[{"utf8":"Yeah; long story short extending the ultrasonic sensor wire is not easily possible."}]},{"tStartMs":411240,"dDurationMs":4320,"segs":[{"utf8":"I mean I tried two different types of shielded wire with thick enough"}]},{"tStartMs":415560,"dDurationMs":7720,"segs":[{"utf8":"conductors and got as close as possible to the sensor itself as well as the driver board."}]},{"tStartMs":423280,"dDurationMs":4120,"segs":[{"utf8":"But not matter what I tried, while using an extension the"}]},{"tStartMs":427400,"dDurationMs":6160,"segs":[{"utf8":"sensor always spat out garbage values. So I am not going to try reverse engineer"}]},{"tStartMs":433560,"dDurationMs":7240,"segs":[{"utf8":"this black magic wire and instead keep it simple by grabbing my backup sensor and using"}]},{"tStartMs":440800,"dDurationMs":8000,"segs":[{"utf8":"an extension cable at the driver board side which I of course tested and it works perfectly fine."}]},{"tStartMs":448800,"dDurationMs":6120,"segs":[{"utf8":"So I grabbed myself a small water resistant junction box that is so small that it fits"}]},{"tStartMs":454920,"dDurationMs":6440,"segs":[{"utf8":"inside the tube, but big enough so that the driver fits inside snugly."}]},{"tStartMs":461360,"dDurationMs":6240,"segs":[{"utf8":"Next I pushed the sensor wire inside there and added a cable bushing on the other side"}]},{"tStartMs":467600,"dDurationMs":8280,"segs":[{"utf8":"through which I pushed my CAT 7 extension cable. And after wiring everything up and closing it up,"}]},{"tStartMs":475880,"dDurationMs":8160,"segs":[{"utf8":"it was time to design an enclosure for the sensor and 3D print that with some PETG filament."}]},{"tStartMs":484040,"dDurationMs":5000,"segs":[{"utf8":"And then it was finally time to do the installation inside the cistern which"}]},{"tStartMs":489040,"dDurationMs":5680,"segs":[{"utf8":"means mounting the enclosure, pushing the sensor in there and then pushing the wire"}]},{"tStartMs":494720,"dDurationMs":6880,"segs":[{"utf8":"and ultimately the junction box inside the tub which worked out beautifully."}]},{"tStartMs":501600,"dDurationMs":5760,"segs":[{"utf8":"Last but not least I connected the driver board extension wires back to a microcontroller to make"}]},{"tStartMs":507360,"dDurationMs":7400,"segs":[{"utf8":"sure that everything still worked and it did. Now at this point we could finish this project"}]},{"tStartMs":514760,"dDurationMs":5360,"segs":[{"utf8":"quickly by simply adding an LCD and calling it a day."}]},{"tStartMs":520120,"dDurationMs":5440,"segs":[{"utf8":"But since I recently created my own Home Assistant Smart Home Control Screen,"}]},{"tStartMs":525560,"dDurationMs":6840,"segs":[{"utf8":"link to the video in the description, I would love to present the water level value on there."}]},{"tStartMs":532400,"dDurationMs":5920,"segs":[{"utf8":"To do that I grabbed myself an ESP microcontroller, flashed the ESP Home"}]},{"tStartMs":538320,"dDurationMs":7080,"segs":[{"utf8":"firmware onto that and then hooked it up to the driver board according to this wiring diagram."}]},{"tStartMs":545400,"dDurationMs":6120,"segs":[{"utf8":"Now the great thing is that ESPHome which is an application for Home Assistant"}]},{"tStartMs":551520,"dDurationMs":6440,"segs":[{"utf8":"actually supports this ultrasonic sensor. The only bad thing is that I had to fish out the"}]},{"tStartMs":557960,"dDurationMs":9240,"segs":[{"utf8":"driver board out of the tube once again in order to add a 47kohm resistor here to enter mode 4"}]},{"tStartMs":567200,"dDurationMs":7080,"segs":[{"utf8":"which is mandatory to make it work with ESP Home. But with that out of the way; I wrote a bit of"}]},{"tStartMs":574280,"dDurationMs":5280,"segs":[{"utf8":"code for my ESP board, uploaded that and thus pretty easily got"}]},{"tStartMs":579560,"dDurationMs":5160,"segs":[{"utf8":"the water level values I was after. That means it was time to finish my"}]},{"tStartMs":584720,"dDurationMs":6760,"segs":[{"utf8":"project and to do that, I installed some conduit in my garage in order to guide the"}]},{"tStartMs":591480,"dDurationMs":6400,"segs":[{"utf8":"extension wire to my big distribution box. Inside there I then added an enclosure for"}]},{"tStartMs":597880,"dDurationMs":5920,"segs":[{"utf8":"the microcontroller as well as a 5V power supply to power it all."}]},{"tStartMs":603800,"dDurationMs":6040,"segs":[{"utf8":"And by the way even though I feel like a broken record here, I have to say that working with"}]},{"tStartMs":609840,"dDurationMs":6080,"segs":[{"utf8":"such mains voltage can be dangerous and should only be done by professionals."}]},{"tStartMs":615920,"dDurationMs":7280,"segs":[{"utf8":"But anyway after the initial wiring was done, I did a small test which turned out successful"}]},{"tStartMs":623200,"dDurationMs":6560,"segs":[{"utf8":"and thus put the microcontroller permanently in its enclosure prison and just like that"}]},{"tStartMs":629760,"dDurationMs":7240,"segs":[{"utf8":"my niche project was complete and functional. And when we do the math and include everything"}]},{"tStartMs":637000,"dDurationMs":7360,"segs":[{"utf8":"that was required for my DIY version then I would say that the price is not too bad."}]},{"tStartMs":644360,"dDurationMs":6360,"segs":[{"utf8":"Now comparing my DIY version to a commercial version is not simple to do though because it"}]},{"tStartMs":650720,"dDurationMs":5560,"segs":[{"utf8":"is very customizable when it comes to the hardware and software side."}]},{"tStartMs":656280,"dDurationMs":4640,"segs":[{"utf8":"But when we compare it to average WiFi solutions out there, then I"}]},{"tStartMs":660920,"dDurationMs":5800,"segs":[{"utf8":"certainly saved quite a bit of money there. And I think that is the beauty when it comes"}]},{"tStartMs":666720,"dDurationMs":6320,"segs":[{"utf8":"to such niche electronics projects because if you have some idea of what you are doing"}]},{"tStartMs":673040,"dDurationMs":6760,"segs":[{"utf8":"then you can certainly save a bit of money while of course investing a bit of your time."}]},{"tStartMs":679800,"dDurationMs":5360,"segs":[{"utf8":"And that is why the winner for me this time is definitely DIY."}]},{"tStartMs":685160,"dDurationMs":4080,"segs":[{"utf8":"But what do you think? Let me know in the comment section below."}]},{"tStartMs":689760,"dDurationMs":5600,"segs":[{"utf8":"As always I hope you enjoyed this video and if you want to see more then consider"}]},{"tStartMs":695360,"dDurationMs":4840,"segs":[{"utf8":"supporting this how on Patreon. Don't forget to like, share,"}]},{"tStartMs":700200,"dDurationMs":9040,"segs":[{"utf8":"subscribe and hit the notification bell. Stay creative and I will see you next time."}]}]}